<title>USA: Rose's Stores Inc Q3 shr profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>Rose's Stores Inc Q3 shr profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>HENDERSON, N.C. 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr profit		 $0.05     loss	 $0.06</p>
<p> Net profit		   448     loss	   480</p>
<p> Sales		    160,796		  162,937</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   8,625		    8,625</p>
<p>	  9   MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $0.19		    $0.00</p>
<p> Net loss		   1,606   profit	    18</p>
<p> Sales		    481,066		  490,832</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   8,625		    8,625</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE - Q3 1996 ended October 26, 1996; Q3 1995 ended October 28, 1995.</p>
<p>The number of shares used in the earnings per share calculations is the amount of stock that will be issued if all pending claims are resolved adversely to the company, it said. If all pending claims are resolved in accordance with the company's records, 8,608 shares will be issued. Currently, 8,460 shares have been distributed.</p>
<p>Results for first nine months of 1995 are pro forma as though company had adopted fresh-start accounting at the beginning of 1995.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
